// [M-imports-entry-folder-module-self-cycle-empty-exports] /
// [M-imports-order-dependent-cycle] regression pair, leg A. Genuine
// two-way import cycle: cyc_a imports cyc_b, cyc_b imports cyc_a back —
// NEITHER file is the CU entry (cycle_test.nv is). D291 (07-modules.md)
// explicitly allows cross-module import cycles ("collect-signatures-first,
// lazy bodies"); [M-imports-order-dependent-cycle] (2026-07-20) generalized
// the entry-exports fix (2026-07-20) to ANY in-progress module, not just
// the CU entry — a module's own exported names are cached as soon as its
// items are parsed, before its own imports are followed, so a cyclic
// back-edge now sees them instead of an empty set. This pair used to be a
// NEGATIVE fixture (compile MUST fail) — now POSITIVE: `cyc_b.b_calls_a`
// (leg B) legitimately resolves `a_val` across the cycle.
module entry_self_cycle.cyc_a

import ./cyc_b.{b_val}

export fn a_val() -> int => b_val() + 1
